        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Combination Therapy"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In many patients with established cardiorenal disease or inadequate glycemic control, clinical guidelines increasingly support combining both an SGLT2 inhibitor and a GLP-1 receptor agonist, as their mechanisms of action and protective benefits are additive rather than overlapping.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          9,
          10
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For detailed guidance tailored to specific health profiles, you can review the American Diabetes Association Standards of Care."
      },
